    {
      "src": "images/cartridges/6-5x55mm-swedish/military-ball.webp",
      "alt": "A 6.5x55mm military ball cartridge with a silvery round-nosed bullet in a copper-washed case, photographed beside a second view of the same case head. The headstamp is quartered by four segments and marked with a crown, the letters O and M, and the figure 6.",
      "caption": "A Swedish 6.5 mm skarp patron m/94 projektil m/94 service round, made at Marieberg in Stockholm, with its headstamp alongside. This is the long round-nose service ball the round was adopted with in 1894; the spitzer m/41 projectile replaced it from 1941.",
